cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both this repository and the paper it
  accompanies. The code is licensed under the GNU GPL, version 3 or later.
title: >-
  Lead I alone carries much of what physicians read on a 12-lead ECG (code)
abstract: >-
  Code, aggregated results and figures for a study of ECG encoders pre-trained with
  self-supervised learning on unlabelled MIMIC-IV-ECG recordings and read out frozen
  with one logistic regression per finding. Strip encoders of one, two and twelve
  leads are evaluated against 13 physician-annotated findings in two external
  twelve-lead cohorts (Chapman-Shaoxing and Ningbo; PTB-XL), on atrial fibrillation
  in handheld single-lead recordings, and on hospital diagnoses of MIMIC-IV patients
  not seen in pre-training; an autoencoder on the averaged heartbeat, reproduced from
  Friedman et al. (2025), is the comparison. Apart from one openly licensed example
  recording for Fig. 1, no ECG data or patient records are included; trained weights
  and the manuscript are not included either.
